# Trivy vulnerability ignore list
# Every entry below is a real, fixed-upstream CVE that this repo cannot remediate
# on its own — the fix lives in a binary we don't compile (a new HA base image for
# tempio, a new ha-cli release for ha) or behind a dependency cap we don't control.
# Review periodically and prune each entry when its stated condition is met.

# --- /usr/bin/tempio (Home Assistant base image templating binary) ---
# Go stdlib + x/crypto CVEs in /usr/bin/tempio, the templating binary baked into
# the Home Assistant base image (built with Go 1.23.3 / x/crypto 0.26.0).
# Not fixable here — tempio is not an apk package and is not recompiled by this
# add-on; only a new HA base image release can resolve these. Re-scan and prune
# when the base image is bumped. Last verified against base:3.24 / 2026.06.1
# (2026-08-04) — tempio is still the 2024.11.2 build, unchanged since 2024-11-26.
CVE-2024-45337
CVE-2025-22869
CVE-2025-61726
CVE-2025-61729
CVE-2025-68121
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
CVE-2026-42504
# Additional tempio x/crypto (ssh/agent/knownhosts) + stdlib crypto/x509 CVEs,
# newly disclosed against the same Go 1.23.3 / x/crypto 0.26.0 build.
CVE-2025-47913
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-39828
CVE-2026-39829
CVE-2026-39830
CVE-2026-39831
CVE-2026-39832
CVE-2026-39835
CVE-2026-42508
CVE-2026-46595
CVE-2026-46597

# --- /usr/bin/ha (Home Assistant CLI) ---
# golang.org/x/net v0.43.0 and x/text v0.28.0 CVEs compiled into the ha-cli
# binary. We already pin HA_CLI_VERSION to the latest release (5.2.0); the fixes
# (x/net >= 0.55.0, x/text >= 0.39.0) require an upstream ha-cli rebuild, so this
# is not fixable by bumping our pin. Prune when a newer ha-cli release links
# x/net >= 0.55.0 and x/text >= 0.39.0. Verified against ha-cli 5.2.0, still the
# latest release (2026-08-04).
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-56852

# --- Go stdlib (both /usr/bin/tempio and /usr/bin/ha) ---
# os.Root symlink-following flaw, fixed in Go 1.25.12. Hits both binaries at once
# (tempio on go1.23.3, ha on go1.25.11) and neither is compiled here, so both an
# HA base image release and an ha-cli release are needed to clear it.
CVE-2026-39822

# --- claude-terminal/ha-mcp/uv.lock (cryptography) ---
# CVE-2026-69247: Bleichenbacher oracle in cryptography's PKCS#7 EnvelopedData
# decryption, fixed in 50.0.0. Not fixable here — ha-mcp caps the dependency at
# `cryptography<50,>=48.0.0` (both the pinned 7.14.2 and the current 8.0.0), so
# `uv lock --upgrade-package cryptography` resolves straight back to 49.0.0.
# Not reachable either: cryptography reaches us via ha-mcp/authlib/joserfc, which
# use JWS/JWE/JWT and X.509 — none of them call the PKCS#7 decrypt path, and the
# add-on never decrypts attacker-supplied PKCS#7 blobs.
# Prune when ha-mcp relaxes the <50 cap and uv.lock picks up cryptography 50.
CVE-2026-69247
